From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: Task View's windows fly into place

David: "when you click the task view, the windows flying into place rather
than a harsh 1 frame change". Opening, each window's thumbnail moves from
where the window is on the screen to its place in the grid over 220 ms,
easing out; clicks and keys use the grid places throughout. Only with "Show
animations in Windows" (SPI_GETCLIENTAREAANIMATION) on, as on Windows.
SG_TASKVIEW_ANIM_MS sets the length (for gates).

Gate: make test-taskview-anim.
--- a/programs/explorer/vdesktop.c
